{#
    One `BaseTree` entity's records, as a tree.

    THE WHOLE TREE IS IN THE DELIVERED HTML, and the module only folds it up — the same rule
    `tabs_controller.js` follows and for the same reason. Nodes hidden in CSS and revealed by
    script would turn a module that fails to load into a tree showing its roots with no sign
    that anything hangs below them. Without JavaScript every node is visible and every link
    works; collapsing is the convenience, not the mechanism.

    THE NESTING IS THE MARKUP, not an indent class. A nested `<ul>` inside the `<li>` it belongs
    to is what makes the structure readable to a screen reader and to the gate; faking depth with
    a padding class would leave both guessing.

    THERE IS DELIBERATELY NO `role="tree"`. That role commits a widget to the full tree keyboard
    specification — arrow keys across every node, a roving `tabindex`, Home and End, type-ahead —
    and a page that announces the role without them is worse off than one that does not: a screen
    reader tells the user to navigate in a way that then does nothing. What this page actually is
    is a nested list of links with a disclosure button per branch, so it says that: `<ul>`, `<a>`
    and a `<button>` carrying `aria-expanded` and `aria-controls`. Native elements, keyboard
    reachable without a line of script. Upgrading to the real widget is a decision of its own.

    THE SWITCH TO THE LIST IS PART OF THE PAGE, not a convenience bolted on. A tree entity has
    exactly one menu entry and it points here (ADR 0025), so this link is the only offered way to
    the filter, the full-text search and the bulk actions of story 002-004. Removing it does not
    remove a feature from this page — it removes one from the entity.

    THE CLASSES THIS GATE READS ARE `admin-tree__switch`, `admin-tree__node` AND
    `admin-tree__label`, and naming them here is load-bearing: `tools/harness-baum-pruefen.php`
    (story 004-001-0006) finds the switch, the nodes and their names by exactly these, the way
    `harness-liste-pruefen.php` reads the table through `admin-list__cell`. Renaming one without
    the gate makes the gate read nothing and stay green.

    A NODE IS CREATED WHERE IT IS CLICKED, and the place travels in the address rather than in a
    hidden field: `node.newChildUrl` is the form of this entity with `treeParent` in the query,
    which `FormController` checks against the tree before it prefills anything. The link at the
    top creates on the root level and carries no parent at all — without it a tree whose roots
    are all someone else's would have no reachable place to add anything.

    THE LABEL MAY BE AN ID, and that is the maintained state of the entity showing through:
    `settings.labelProperty` defaults to null (gap L6) and `TreeController::labelProperty()`
    answers that with the record's id rather than a guessed field (ADR 0016).
#}{% extends 'layout.html.twig' %}

{% block bodyAttributes %} class="admin"{% endblock %}

{% macro branch(nodes) %}
    <ul class="admin-tree__list">
{% for node in nodes %}
        <li class="admin-tree__node">
            <div class="admin-tree__row">
{% if node.childs is not empty %}
                <button type="button" class="admin-tree__toggle"
                        aria-expanded="true"
                        aria-controls="tree-childs-{{ node.id }}"
                        data-action="admin-tree#toggle"
                        data-admin-tree-target="toggle">
                    <span class="admin-tree__toggle-sign" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                    <span class="admin-tree__toggle-text">{{ node.label }} zuklappen</span>
                </button>
{% endif %}
                <a class="admin-tree__label" href="{{ node.url }}">{{ node.label }}</a>
                <a class="admin-tree__add" href="{{ node.newChildUrl }}"
                   title="Unterknoten unter {{ node.label }} anlegen">Unterknoten anlegen</a>
            </div>
{% if node.childs is not empty %}
            <div class="admin-tree__childs" id="tree-childs-{{ node.id }}"
                 data-admin-tree-target="childs" data-admin-tree-node="{{ node.id }}">
{{ _self.branch(node.childs) }}
            </div>
{% endif %}
        </li>
{% endfor %}
    </ul>
{% endmacro %}

{% block content %}
<main class="admin__main">
    <h1>{{ entity }}</h1>

    <p class="admin-tree__new"><a href="{{ newUrl }}">Neuer Knoten auf oberster Ebene</a></p>

    <p class="admin-tree__switch"><a href="{{ listUrl }}">Als Liste anzeigen</a></p>

{% if nodes is empty %}
    <p class="admin-tree__empty">Für diese Datenart gibt es noch keine Einträge.</p>
{% else %}
    <div class="admin-tree" data-controller="admin-tree"
         data-admin-tree-entity-value="{{ entity }}">
{{ _self.branch(nodes) }}
    </div>
{% endif %}
</main>
{% endblock %}
